IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc1-common`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Part 2, entitlement: the minimum age (regulation 8) and being in
-- Great Britain (regulations 9 to 11).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit, alone or as one of a couple.
--
-- The basic conditions are section 4 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012, which is not among the inputs: the conditions "at least 18
-- years old" and "in Great Britain" are named by the text of these regulations, and the rest of section 4 is outside this module.
-- Facts that other provisions decide stay plain inputs, commented where it matters: limited capability for work and the Part 5
-- assessment (piece uc4), the EEA Regulations and the immigration rules (other instruments), and regulation 30's caring
-- responsibilities (uc1-part4-needs.l4).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 8: cases where the minimum age is 16.

-- (4) "Care leaver": in relation to England, an eligible child for paragraph 19B of Schedule 2 to the Children Act 1989 or a relevant
-- child for section 23A of that Act; in relation to Scotland, a person under 18 who is looked after by a local authority, or has
-- ceased to be looked after but is owed advice and assistance under section 29(1) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 or is provided
-- with continuing care under section 26A of it, and who since 14 has been looked after for 3 months or more in all (not counting a
-- placement with family); in relation to Wales, a category 1 or category 2 young person.
-- src:207 | “care leaver” means—
-- src:208 | (a) in relation to England..., an eligible child for the purposes of paragraph 19B of Schedule 2 to the Children Act 1989 or a relevant child for the purposes of section 23A of that Act;
-- src:209 | (b) in relation to Scotland, a person under the age of 18 who—
-- src:210 | (i) is looked after by a local authority; or
-- src:211 | (ii) has ceased to be looked after by a local authority but is a person to whom a local authority in Scotland is obliged to provide advice and assistance in terms of section 29(1) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 or a person who is being provided with continuing care under section 26A of that Act,
-- src:212 | and who, since reaching the age of 14 has been looked after by a local authority for a period of, or periods totalling, 3 months or more (excluding any period where the person has been placed with a member of their family);
-- src:213 | (c) in relation to Wales, a category 1 young person or category 2 young person within the meaning of section 104(2) of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014.
@ref reg 8(4) (src:207-213)
DECLARE `Young person who may be a care leaver` HAS
    `nation in which the care is provided`                                                                          IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
    `the person is an eligible child for the purposes of paragraph 19B of Schedule 2 to the Children Act 1989, or a relevant child for the purposes of section 23A of that Act`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts on children (not a piece)
    `the person is under the age of 18`                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is looked after by a local authority`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has ceased to be looked after by a local authority but is a person to whom a local authority in Scotland is obliged to provide advice and assistance in terms of section 29(1) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995, or is being provided with continuing care under section 26A of that Act`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts on children (not a piece)
    `since reaching the age of 14 the person has been looked after by a local authority for a period of, or periods totalling, 3 months or more, excluding any period where the person has been placed with a member of their family`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a category 1 young person or category 2 young person within the meaning of section 104(2) of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts on children (not a piece)

-- src:207 | “care leaver” means—
-- src:208 | (a) in relation to England..., an eligible child for the purposes of paragraph 19B of Schedule 2 to the Children Act 1989 or a relevant child for the purposes of section 23A of that Act;
-- src:209 | (b) in relation to Scotland, a person under the age of 18 who—
-- src:210 | (i) is looked after by a local authority; or
-- src:211 | (ii) has ceased to be looked after by a local authority but is a person to whom a local authority in Scotland is obliged to provide advice and assistance in terms of section 29(1) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 or a person who is being provided with continuing care under section 26A of that Act,
-- src:212 | and who, since reaching the age of 14 has been looked after by a local authority for a period of, or periods totalling, 3 months or more (excluding any period where the person has been placed with a member of their family);
-- src:213 | (c) in relation to Wales, a category 1 young person or category 2 young person within the meaning of section 104(2) of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014.
@ref reg 8(4) (src:207-213)
GIVEN person IS A `Young person who may be a care leaver`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 8(4) — the person is a care leaver` person MEANS
    CONSIDER person's `nation in which the care is provided`
    WHEN England THEN person's `the person is an eligible child for the purposes of paragraph 19B of Schedule 2 to the Children Act 1989, or a relevant child for the purposes of section 23A of that Act`
    WHEN Wales THEN person's `the person is a category 1 young person or category 2 young person within the meaning of section 104(2) of the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014`
    WHEN Scotland THEN
        (person's `the person is under the age of 18`)
        AND ((person's `the person is looked after by a local authority`)
             OR (person's `the person has ceased to be looked after by a local authority but is a person to whom a local authority in Scotland is obliged to provide advice and assistance in terms of section 29(1) of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995, or is being provided with continuing care under section 26A of that Act`))
        AND (person's `since reaching the age of 14 the person has been looked after by a local authority for a period of, or periods totalling, 3 months or more, excluding any period where the person has been placed with a member of their family`)

-- (4) "Confinement": labour resulting in the birth of a living child, or labour after 24 weeks of pregnancy resulting in the birth of
-- a child whether alive or dead; where labour begun on one day results in a birth on another, the woman is confined on the date of
-- the birth. The seat gives the date of the birth.
-- src:214 | “confinement” means—
-- src:215 | (a) labour resulting in the birth of a living child; or
-- src:216 | (b) labour after 24 weeks of pregnancy resulting in the birth of a child whether alive or dead, and where a woman's labour begun on one day results in the birth of a child on another day she is to be taken to be confined on the date of the birth.
@ref reg 8(4) (src:214-216)
GIVEN `labour resulted in the birth of a living child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `labour after 24 weeks of pregnancy resulted in the birth of a child, whether alive or dead` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 8(4) — a confinement` `labour resulted in the birth of a living child` `labour after 24 weeks of pregnancy resulted in the birth of a child, whether alive or dead` MEANS
    (`labour resulted in the birth of a living child`)
    OR (`labour after 24 weeks of pregnancy resulted in the birth of a child, whether alive or dead`)

-- (1)(f) The person is pregnant, and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or was pregnant and it is
-- 15 weeks or less since the date of her confinement. Weeks are counted in days (11 weeks is 77 days, 15 weeks 105 days) from the
-- first day of the expected week and from the date of confinement (fork F-8-WEEKS). A person still pregnant on or after the first
-- day of the expected week is read as within the first limb (fork F-8-OVERDUE): the text gives no upper end for a pregnancy that
-- runs past the expected week.
-- src:193 | (f) is pregnant, and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or was pregnant and it is 15 weeks or less since the date of her confinement; or
@ref reg 8(1)(f) (src:193)
DECLARE `Pregnancy of a person` HAS
    `first day of the expected week of confinement, if the person is pregnant`  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date of confinement, if the person was pregnant and has been confined`      IS A MAYBE DATE

-- src:193 | (f) is pregnant, and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or was pregnant and it is 15 weeks or less since the date of her confinement; or
@ref reg 8(1)(f) (src:193)
GIVEN pregnancy IS A `Pregnancy of a person`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 8(1)(f) — pregnant or recently confined on a day` pregnancy day MEANS
    `within 11 weeks before the expected week of confinement or after it`
    OR `within 15 weeks since the confinement`
    WHERE
        `within 11 weeks before the expected week of confinement or after it` MEANS
            CONSIDER pregnancy's `first day of the expected week of confinement, if the person is pregnant`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST expected THEN ((Day expected) MINUS (Day day)) AT MOST 77
        `within 15 weeks since the confinement` MEANS
            CONSIDER pregnancy's `date of confinement, if the person was pregnant and has been confined`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST confined THEN (((Day day) MINUS (Day confined)) AT LEAST 0) AND (((Day day) MINUS (Day confined)) AT MOST 105)

-- (3)(c) The person is living away from their parents, and neither parent is able to support the person financially because that
-- parent has a physical or mental impairment, is detained in custody pending trial or sentence (or under a sentence), or is
-- prohibited from entering or re-entering Great Britain. "Parent" includes any person acting in the place of a parent (paragraph (4)).
-- src:201 | (c) is living away from their parents, and neither parent is able to support the person financially because that parent—
-- src:202 | (i) has a physical or mental impairment,
-- src:203 | (ii) is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction or under a sentence imposed by a court, or
-- src:204 | (iii) is prohibited from entering or re-entering Great Britain.
@ref reg 8(3)(c) (src:201-204)
DECLARE `Parent of a young person` HAS
    `the parent has a physical or mental impairment`                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parent is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction or under a sentence imposed by a court`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parent is prohibited from entering or re-entering Great Britain`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:201 | (c) is living away from their parents, and neither parent is able to support the person financially because that parent—
-- src:202 | (i) has a physical or mental impairment,
-- src:203 | (ii) is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction or under a sentence imposed by a court, or
-- src:204 | (iii) is prohibited from entering or re-entering Great Britain.
@ref reg 8(3)(c) (src:201-204)
GIVEN parent IS A `Parent of a young person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 8(3)(c) — the parent is unable to support the person financially` parent MEANS
    (parent's `the parent has a physical or mental impairment`)
    OR (parent's `the parent is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction or under a sentence imposed by a court`)
    OR (parent's `the parent is prohibited from entering or re-entering Great Britain`)

-- (3) A young person is without parental support where they are not being looked after by a local authority and (a) have no parent;
-- (b) cannot live with their parents because they are estranged from them or there is a serious risk to their physical or mental
-- health, or that they would suffer significant harm, if they lived with them; or (c) are living away from their parents and neither
-- parent is able to support them financially for one of the reasons in (c)(i) to (iii).
-- src:196 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(g) a young person is without parental support where that person is not being looked after by a local authority and—
-- src:197 | (a) has no parent;
-- src:198 | (b) cannot live with their parents because—
-- src:199 | (i) the person is estranged from them, or
-- src:200 | (ii) there is a serious risk to the person's physical or mental health, or that the person would suffer significant harm if the person lived with them; or
-- src:201 | (c) is living away from their parents, and neither parent is able to support the person financially because that parent—
-- src:202 | (i) has a physical or mental impairment,
-- src:203 | (ii) is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction or under a sentence imposed by a court, or
-- src:204 | (iii) is prohibited from entering or re-entering Great Britain.
@ref reg 8(3) (src:196-204)
DECLARE `Young person who may be without parental support` HAS
    `the person is being looked after by a local authority`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has no parent`                                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person cannot live with their parents because the person is estranged from them`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person cannot live with their parents because there is a serious risk to the person's physical or mental health, or that the person would suffer significant harm if the person lived with them`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts on detention in hospital (not a piece)
    `the person is living away from their parents`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's parents`                                                                                              IS A LIST OF `Parent of a young person`

-- src:196 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(g) a young person is without parental support where that person is not being looked after by a local authority and—
-- src:197 | (a) has no parent;
-- src:198 | (b) cannot live with their parents because—
-- src:199 | (i) the person is estranged from them, or
-- src:200 | (ii) there is a serious risk to the person's physical or mental health, or that the person would suffer significant harm if the person lived with them; or
-- src:201 | (c) is living away from their parents, and neither parent is able to support the person financially because that parent—
-- src:202 | (i) has a physical or mental impairment,
-- src:203 | (ii) is detained in custody pending trial or sentence upon conviction or under a sentence imposed by a court, or
-- src:204 | (iii) is prohibited from entering or re-entering Great Britain.
@ref reg 8(3) (src:196-204)
GIVEN person IS A `Young person who may be without parental support`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 8(3) — the person is without parental support` person MEANS
    (NOT (person's `the person is being looked after by a local authority`))
    AND (`limb (a)` OR `limb (b)` OR `limb (c)`)
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS person's `the person has no parent`
        `limb (b)` MEANS
            (person's `the person cannot live with their parents because the person is estranged from them`)
            OR (person's `the person cannot live with their parents because there is a serious risk to the person's physical or mental health, or that the person would suffer significant harm if the person lived with them`)
        `limb (c)` MEANS
            (person's `the person is living away from their parents`)
            AND (all (GIVEN parent YIELD `reg 8(3)(c) — the parent is unable to support the person financially` parent) (person's `the person's parents`))

-- (1) The minimum age is 16 where a person (a) has limited capability for work; (b) is awaiting an assessment under Part 5 and has a
-- statement under the Medical Evidence Regulations that they are not fit for work; (c) has regular and substantial caring
-- responsibilities for a severely disabled person; (d) is responsible for a child; (e) is a member of a couple whose other member is
-- responsible for a child or qualifying young person (only where the other member meets the basic conditions in section 4); (f) is
-- pregnant or was recently confined; or (g) is without parental support. (2) Limbs (c), (f) and (g) do not include a care leaver.
-- src:187 | (1) For the basic condition in section 4(1)(a) of the Act (at least 18 years old), the minimum age is 16 years old where a person—
-- src:188 | (a) has limited capability for work;
-- src:189 | (b) is awaiting an assessment under Part 5 to determine whether the person has limited capability for work and has a statement given ... in accordance with the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work;
-- src:190 | (c) has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person;
-- src:191 | (d) is responsible for a child;
-- src:192 | (e) is a member of a couple the other member of which is responsible for a child or a qualifying young person (but only where the other member meets the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act);
-- src:193 | (f) is pregnant, and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or was pregnant and it is 15 weeks or less since the date of her confinement; or
-- src:194 | (g) is without parental support (see paragraph (3)).
-- src:195 | (2) Sub-paragraphs (c), (f) and (g) of paragraph (1) do not include any person who is a care leaver.
@ref reg 8(1) and (2) (src:187-195)
DECLARE `Person who may have the minimum age of 16` HAS
    `the person has limited capability for work`                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Part 5 (piece uc4)
    `the person is awaiting an assessment under Part 5 to determine whether the person has limited capability for work`        IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Part 5 (piece uc4)
    `the person has a statement given in accordance with the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Medical Evidence Regulations (not a piece)
    `the person has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is responsible for a child`                                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a member of a couple the other member of which is responsible for a child or a qualifying young person`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other member meets the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Act, sections 4, 5 or 22 (not a piece)
    `the person is pregnant, and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or was pregnant and it is 15 weeks or less since the date of her confinement`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is without parental support`                                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a care leaver`                                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:187 | (1) For the basic condition in section 4(1)(a) of the Act (at least 18 years old), the minimum age is 16 years old where a person—
-- src:188 | (a) has limited capability for work;
-- src:189 | (b) is awaiting an assessment under Part 5 to determine whether the person has limited capability for work and has a statement given ... in accordance with the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work;
-- src:190 | (c) has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person;
-- src:191 | (d) is responsible for a child;
-- src:192 | (e) is a member of a couple the other member of which is responsible for a child or a qualifying young person (but only where the other member meets the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act);
-- src:193 | (f) is pregnant, and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or was pregnant and it is 15 weeks or less since the date of her confinement; or
-- src:194 | (g) is without parental support (see paragraph (3)).
-- src:195 | (2) Sub-paragraphs (c), (f) and (g) of paragraph (1) do not include any person who is a care leaver.
@ref reg 8(1) and (2) (src:187-195)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may have the minimum age of 16`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 8(1) — the minimum age is 16` person MEANS
    (person's `the person has limited capability for work`)
    OR `limb (b)`
    OR `limb (c)`
    OR (person's `the person is responsible for a child`)
    OR `limb (e)`
    OR `limb (f)`
    OR `limb (g)`
    WHERE
        `limb (b)` MEANS
            (person's `the person is awaiting an assessment under Part 5 to determine whether the person has limited capability for work`)
            AND (person's `the person has a statement given in accordance with the Medical Evidence Regulations which provides that the person is not fit for work`)
        `limb (c)` MEANS
            (person's `the person has regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person`)
            AND (NOT (person's `the person is a care leaver`))
        `limb (e)` MEANS
            (person's `the person is a member of a couple the other member of which is responsible for a child or a qualifying young person`)
            AND (person's `the other member meets the basic conditions in section 4 of the Act`)
        `limb (f)` MEANS
            (person's `the person is pregnant, and it is 11 weeks or less before her expected week of confinement, or was pregnant and it is 15 weeks or less since the date of her confinement`)
            AND (NOT (person's `the person is a care leaver`))
        `limb (g)` MEANS
            (person's `the person is without parental support`)
            AND (NOT (person's `the person is a care leaver`))

-- The basic condition in section 4(1)(a) of the Act is "at least 18 years old" (the text puts it so in paragraph (1)); where the
-- minimum age is 16 the person needs to be at least 16.
-- src:187 | (1) For the basic condition in section 4(1)(a) of the Act (at least 18 years old), the minimum age is 16 years old where a person—
@ref reg 8(1) (src:187)
GIVEN `the minimum age is 16` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 8 — the minimum age` `the minimum age is 16` MEANS
    IF `the minimum age is 16` THEN 16 ELSE 18

-- src:187 | (1) For the basic condition in section 4(1)(a) of the Act (at least 18 years old), the minimum age is 16 years old where a person—
@ref reg 8(1) (src:187)
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the age is asked` IS A DATE
      `the minimum age is 16` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 8 — the person meets the basic condition on age` `date of birth` `the day on which the age is asked` `the minimum age is 16` MEANS
    (`uc1 — the age in complete years on a date` `date of birth` `the day on which the age is asked`)
        AT LEAST (`reg 8 — the minimum age` `the minimum age is 16`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 9: persons treated as not being in Great Britain.

-- (3), (3A) A right to reside that does not count: one that exists by virtue of, or in accordance with, regulation 13 of the EEA
-- Regulations; regulation 14, only where the person is a jobseeker or a family member of one; regulation 16, only where the person
-- satisfies the criteria in regulation 16(5); or limited leave under Appendix EU (but see (3A)), as a person with a Zambrano right,
-- or with an Appendix EU (Family Permit) entry clearance.
-- src:221 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2), a right to reside does not include a right which exists by virtue of, or in accordance with—
-- src:222 | (a) regulation 13 of the EEA Regulations ...; ...
-- src:223 | (aa) regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations, but only in cases where the right exists under that regulation because the person is–
-- src:224 | (i) a qualified person for the purposes of regulation 6(1) of those Regulations as a jobseeker; or
-- src:225 | (ii) a family member (within the meaning of regulation 7 of those Regulations) of such a jobseeker; ...
-- src:226 | (b) regulation 16 of the EEA Regulations, but only in cases where the right exists under that regulation because the person satisfies the criteria in regulation 16(5) of those Regulations ...; or
-- src:227 | (c) a person having been granted limited leave to enter, or remain in, the United Kingdom under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of—
-- src:228 | (i) Appendix EU to the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act; ...
-- src:229 | (ii) being a person with a Zambrano right to reside as defined in Annex 1 of Appendix EU to the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act; or
-- src:230 | (iii) having arrived in the United Kingdom with an entry clearance that was granted under Appendix EU (Family Permit) to the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act.
-- src:231 | (3A) Paragraph (3)(c)(i) does not apply to a person who—
-- src:232 | (a) has a right to reside granted by virtue of being a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland; and
-- src:233 | (b) would have a right to reside under the EEA Regulations if the relevant person of Northern Ireland were an EEA national, provided that the right to reside does not fall within paragraph (3)(a) or (b)
@ref reg 9(3) and (3A) (src:221-233)
DECLARE `Right to reside` HAS
    `the right exists by virtue of, or in accordance with, regulation 13 of the EEA Regulations`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: immigration law and the EEA Regulations (not a piece)
    `the right exists under regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because the person is a qualified person for the purposes of regulation 6(1) of those Regulations as a jobseeker`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: immigration law and the EEA Regulations (not a piece)
    `the right exists under regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because the person is a family member of such a jobseeker`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: immigration law and the EEA Regulations (not a piece)
    `the right exists under regulation 16 of the EEA Regulations only because the person satisfies the criteria in regulation 16(5) of those Regulations`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: immigration law and the EEA Regulations (not a piece)
    `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of Appendix EU to the immigration rules`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: immigration law and the EEA Regulations (not a piece)
    `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of being a person with a Zambrano right to reside as defined in Annex 1 of Appendix EU`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: immigration law and the EEA Regulations (not a piece)
    `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of having arrived in the United Kingdom with an entry clearance that was granted under Appendix EU (Family Permit)`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: immigration law and the EEA Regulations (not a piece)
    `the right was granted by virtue of being a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person would have a right to reside under the EEA Regulations if the relevant person of Northern Ireland were an EEA national`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: immigration law and the EEA Regulations (not a piece)
    `that right to reside would fall within paragraph (3)(a) or (b)`                             IS A BOOLEAN

-- (3A) Paragraph (3)(c)(i) does not apply to a person with a right granted by virtue of being a family member of a relevant person of
-- Northern Ireland who would have a right to reside under the EEA Regulations if that person were an EEA national, provided that
-- the right does not fall within (3)(a) or (b).
-- src:231 | (3A) Paragraph (3)(c)(i) does not apply to a person who—
-- src:232 | (a) has a right to reside granted by virtue of being a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland; and
-- src:233 | (b) would have a right to reside under the EEA Regulations if the relevant person of Northern Ireland were an EEA national, provided that the right to reside does not fall within paragraph (3)(a) or (b)
@ref reg 9(3A) (src:231-233)
GIVEN right IS A `Right to reside`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 9(3A) — paragraph (3)(c)(i) does not apply to the right` right MEANS
    (right's `the right was granted by virtue of being a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland`)
    AND (right's `the person would have a right to reside under the EEA Regulations if the relevant person of Northern Ireland were an EEA national`)
    AND (NOT (right's `that right to reside would fall within paragraph (3)(a) or (b)`))

-- src:221 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2), a right to reside does not include a right which exists by virtue of, or in accordance with—
-- src:222 | (a) regulation 13 of the EEA Regulations ...; ...
-- src:223 | (aa) regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations, but only in cases where the right exists under that regulation because the person is–
-- src:224 | (i) a qualified person for the purposes of regulation 6(1) of those Regulations as a jobseeker; or
-- src:225 | (ii) a family member (within the meaning of regulation 7 of those Regulations) of such a jobseeker; ...
-- src:226 | (b) regulation 16 of the EEA Regulations, but only in cases where the right exists under that regulation because the person satisfies the criteria in regulation 16(5) of those Regulations ...; or
-- src:227 | (c) a person having been granted limited leave to enter, or remain in, the United Kingdom under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of—
-- src:228 | (i) Appendix EU to the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act; ...
-- src:229 | (ii) being a person with a Zambrano right to reside as defined in Annex 1 of Appendix EU to the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act; or
-- src:230 | (iii) having arrived in the United Kingdom with an entry clearance that was granted under Appendix EU (Family Permit) to the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act.
@ref reg 9(3) (src:221-230)
GIVEN right IS A `Right to reside`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 9(3) — the right to reside does not count` right MEANS
    (right's `the right exists by virtue of, or in accordance with, regulation 13 of the EEA Regulations`)
    OR (right's `the right exists under regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because the person is a qualified person for the purposes of regulation 6(1) of those Regulations as a jobseeker`)
    OR (right's `the right exists under regulation 14 of the EEA Regulations only because the person is a family member of such a jobseeker`)
    OR (right's `the right exists under regulation 16 of the EEA Regulations only because the person satisfies the criteria in regulation 16(5) of those Regulations`)
    OR (`reg 9(3)(c)(i) — limited leave by virtue of Appendix EU counts against the right` right)
    OR (right's `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of being a person with a Zambrano right to reside as defined in Annex 1 of Appendix EU`)
    OR (right's `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of having arrived in the United Kingdom with an entry clearance that was granted under Appendix EU (Family Permit)`)

-- src:228 | (i) Appendix EU to the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act; ...
@ref reg 9(3)(c)(i) (src:228)
GIVEN right IS A `Right to reside`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 9(3)(c)(i) — limited leave by virtue of Appendix EU counts against the right` right MEANS
    (right's `the person has been granted limited leave under the Immigration Act 1971 by virtue of Appendix EU to the immigration rules`)
    AND (NOT (`reg 9(3A) — paragraph (3)(c)(i) does not apply to the right` right))

