`reg 9(2) — the person has a right to reside that counts` rights MEANS
    any (GIVEN right YIELD NOT (`reg 9(3) — the right to reside does not count` right)) rights

-- (4)(za) to (zg) Persons who are not treated as outside Great Britain: leave granted by virtue of the Afghan Relocations and
-- Assistance Policy or the ex-gratia scheme; a person who left Afghanistan on the collapse of its government; a person who left
-- Ukraine, Sudan or Israel and the surrounding region (each with a leave or a right of abode or no need for leave); a person who left
-- a country from which British nationals were advised to leave or evacuated; a person with leave on a safe and legal humanitarian
-- route.
