-- (zf) A person who was residing outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government advised British nationals to leave or
-- arranged their evacuation, has left and is present in Great Britain, and has a right of abode, no requirement of leave, leave under
-- the rules or leave on a discretionary basis.
-- src:251 | (zf) a person who—
-- src:252 | (i) was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty’s Government—
-- src:253 | (aa) provided public information to advise British nationals to leave that country or territory, or
-- src:254 | (bb) arranged the evacuation of British nationals from that country or territory;
-- src:255 | (ii) has left that country or territory and is present in Great Britain; and
-- src:256 | (iii) has—
-- src:257 | (aa) a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971,
-- src:258 | (bb) no requirement of leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act,
-- src:259 | (cc) leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act, or
-- src:260 | (dd) leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules made under section 3(2) of that Act; or
@ref reg 9(4)(zf) (src:251-260)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be within regulation 9(4)(za) to (zg)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 9(4)(zf) — a person who left a country from which British nationals were advised to leave or evacuated` person MEANS
    (person's `the person was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it, or arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it`)
    AND (person's `the person has left that country or territory and is present in Great Britain`)
    AND ((person's `the person has a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971`)
         OR (person's `the person does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of the Immigration Act 1971`)
         OR (person's `the person has been granted leave in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971`)
         OR (person's `the person has leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971`))

-- (4A) A person within (4)(zf) is treated as in Great Britain for the 6 months beginning on the day the public information is issued or
-- the evacuation starts. The 6 months end the day before the same day 6 months on (fork F-6-MONTHS, the same convention as for
-- regulation 27A(2)).
-- src:272 | (4A) A person who falls within paragraph (4)(zf) will be treated as a person in Great Britain in the circumstances specified in paragraph (1) for 6 months beginning on the day on which the public information is issued, or the evacuation is started.
@ref reg 9(4A) (src:272)
GIVEN `day on which the public information is issued, or the evacuation is started` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 9(4A) — the day is within the 6 months for a person within paragraph (4)(zf)` `day on which the public information is issued, or the evacuation is started` day MEANS
    (day AT LEAST `day on which the public information is issued, or the evacuation is started`)
    AND (day AT MOST ((`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` `day on which the public information is issued, or the evacuation is started` (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months)) MINUS 1))

