-- src:269 | (e) a person who has been granted, or who is deemed to have been granted, leave outside the rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971 ...
-- src:270 | (f) a person who has humanitarian protection granted under those rules; or
-- src:271 | (g) a person who is not a person subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 and who is in the United Kingdom as a result of their deportation, expulsion or other removal by compulsion of law from another country to the United Kingdom.
@ref reg 9(4)(a) to (g) (src:262-271)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be within the remaining limbs of regulation 9(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 9(4)(a) to (g) — the person is within one of the remaining limbs` person MEANS
    (person's `the person is a qualified person for the purposes of regulation 6 of the EEA Regulations as a worker or a self-employed person`)
    OR (person's `the person is a family member of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (a)`)
    OR (person's `the person has a right to reside permanently in the United Kingdom by virtue of regulation 15(1)(c), (d) or (e) of the EEA Regulations`)
    OR ((person's `the person is a family member of a relevant person of Northern Ireland, with a right to reside which falls within paragraph (3)(c)(i)`)
        AND (person's `the relevant person of Northern Ireland falls within paragraph (4)(a), or would do so but for the fact that they are not an EEA national`))
    OR (person's `the person is a frontier worker within the meaning of regulation 3 of the Citizens' Rights (Frontier Workers) (EU Exit) Regulations 2020`)
    OR ((person's `the person is a family member of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (cb)`)
        AND (person's `the person has been granted limited leave to enter, or remain in, the United Kingdom by virtue of Appendix EU to the immigration rules made under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971`))
    OR (person's `the person is a refugee within the definition in Article 1 of the Convention relating to the Status of Refugees done at Geneva on 28th July 1951, as extended by Article 1(2) of the Protocol relating to the Status of Refugees done at New York on 31st January 1967`)
    OR (person's `the person has humanitarian protection granted under the immigration rules`)
    OR (person's `the person is not a person subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9) of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 and is in the United Kingdom as a result of their deportation, expulsion or other removal by compulsion of law from another country to the United Kingdom`)

-- (4) A person falls within paragraph (4) if within any of the limbs above. (4)(e) is read here as one of the first set; the
-- (zf) limb applies on a day only when paragraph (4A)'s 6 months have not run out.
-- src:234 | (4) A person falls within this paragraph if the person is—
@ref reg 9(4) (src:234)
GIVEN `within (za)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within (zb)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within (zc)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within (zd)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within (ze)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within (zf), and the day is within the 6 months of paragraph (4A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within (zg)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within one of the other limbs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 9(4) — the person falls within this paragraph` `within (za)` `within (zb)` `within (zc)` `within (zd)` `within (ze)` `within (zf), and the day is within the 6 months of paragraph (4A)` `within (zg)` `within (e)` `within one of the other limbs` MEANS
    `within (za)`
    OR `within (zb)`
    OR `within (zc)`
    OR `within (zd)`
    OR `within (ze)`
    OR `within (zf), and the day is within the 6 months of paragraph (4A)`
    OR `within (zg)`
    OR `within (e)`
    OR `within one of the other limbs`

-- (1) A person is treated as not being in Great Britain if not habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands, the
-- Isle of Man or the Republic of Ireland (and by paragraph (2) not so resident without a right to reside that counts), except where
-- they fall within paragraph (4).
-- src:219 | (1) For the purposes of determining whether a person meets the basic condition to be in Great Britain, except where a person falls within paragraph (4) and subject to paragraph (4A), a person is to be treated as not being in Great Britain if the person is not habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands, the Isle of Man or the Republic of Ireland.
@ref reg 9(1) (src:219)
GIVEN `the person is habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands, the Isle of Man or the Republic of Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a right to reside that counts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person falls within paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 9(1) — the person is treated as not being in Great Britain` `the person is habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands, the Isle of Man or the Republic of Ireland` `the person has a right to reside that counts` `the person falls within paragraph (4)` MEANS
    (NOT ((`the person is habitually resident in the United Kingdom, the Channel Islands, the Isle of Man or the Republic of Ireland`)
          AND (`the person has a right to reside that counts`)))
    AND (NOT `the person falls within paragraph (4)`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 10: Crown servants and members of Her Majesty's forces posted overseas.

-- (1)(a), (2), (3) A Crown servant (a person holding an office or employment under the Crown) or a member of Her Majesty's forces,
-- performing overseas the duties of one and, immediately before the posting or the first of consecutive postings, habitually
-- resident in the United Kingdom, is posted overseas.
-- src:279 | (a) a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces posted overseas;
-- src:280 | (b) in the case of joint claimants, the partner of a person mentioned in sub-paragraph (a) while they are accompanying the person on that posting.
-- src:281 | (2) A person mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) is posted overseas if the person is performing overseas the duties of a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces and was, immediately before their posting or the first of consecutive postings, habitually resident in the United Kingdom.
-- src:282 | (3) In this regulation—
-- src:283 | “Crown servant” means a person holding an office or employment under the Crown; and
-- src:284 | “Her Majesty's forces” has the meaning in the Armed Forces Act 2006 .
@ref reg 10(1)(a), (2) and (3) (src:279-284)
DECLARE `Person who may be posted overseas` HAS
    `the person holds an office or employment under the Crown`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a member of Her Majesty's forces within the meaning of the Armed Forces Act 2006`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts and Regulations (not a piece)
    `the person is performing overseas the duties of a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was, immediately before their posting or the first of consecutive postings, habitually resident in the United Kingdom`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:279 | (a) a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces posted overseas;
-- src:280 | (b) in the case of joint claimants, the partner of a person mentioned in sub-paragraph (a) while they are accompanying the person on that posting.
-- src:281 | (2) A person mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) is posted overseas if the person is performing overseas the duties of a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces and was, immediately before their posting or the first of consecutive postings, habitually resident in the United Kingdom.
-- src:282 | (3) In this regulation—
-- src:283 | “Crown servant” means a person holding an office or employment under the Crown; and
-- src:284 | “Her Majesty's forces” has the meaning in the Armed Forces Act 2006 .
@ref reg 10(1)(a), (2) and (3) (src:279-284)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be posted overseas`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 10(1)(a) — a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces posted overseas` person MEANS
    `a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces`
    AND (person's `the person is performing overseas the duties of a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces`)
    AND (person's `the person was, immediately before their posting or the first of consecutive postings, habitually resident in the United Kingdom`)
    WHERE
        `a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces` MEANS
            (person's `the person holds an office or employment under the Crown`)
            OR (person's `the person is a member of Her Majesty's forces within the meaning of the Armed Forces Act 2006`)

-- (1) The following do not have to meet the basic condition to be in Great Britain: (a) such a person; (b) in the case of joint
-- claimants, the partner of such a person while accompanying them on that posting.
-- src:278 | (1) The following persons do not have to meet the basic condition to be in Great Britain—
-- src:279 | (a) a Crown servant or member of Her Majesty's forces posted overseas;
-- src:280 | (b) in the case of joint claimants, the partner of a person mentioned in sub-paragraph (a) while they are accompanying the person on that posting.
@ref reg 10(1) (src:278-280)
GIVEN `the person is posted overseas` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is a joint claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partner is posted overseas` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is accompanying the partner on that posting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 10(1) — the person does not have to meet the basic condition to be in Great Britain` `the person is posted overseas` `the claim is a joint claim` `the partner is posted overseas` `the person is accompanying the partner on that posting` MEANS
    (`the person is posted overseas`)
    OR ((`the claim is a joint claim`)
        AND (`the partner is posted overseas`)
        AND (`the person is accompanying the partner on that posting`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 11: temporary absence from Great Britain.

-- (2) The period of one month may be extended by up to a further month if the absence is in connection with the death of the person's
-- partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom the person was responsible, or of a close relative of the person, of their
-- partner or of such a child or young person, and the Secretary of State considers it would be unreasonable to expect the person to
-- return within the first month.
-- src:292 | (2) The period of one month in paragraph (1)(b) may be extended by up to a further month if the temporary absence is in connection with the death of—
-- src:293 | (a) the person's partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom the person was responsible; or
-- src:294 | (b) a close relative of the person, or of their partner or of a child or qualifying young person for whom the person or their partner was responsible,
-- src:295 | and the Secretary of State considers that it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return to Great Britain within the first month.
@ref reg 11(2) (src:292-295)
GIVEN `the absence is in connection with the death of the person's partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom the person was responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the absence is in connection with the death of a close relative of the person, or of their partner or of a child or qualifying young person for whom the person or their partner was responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State considers that it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return to Great Britain within the first month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 11(2) — the months of absence that may be disregarded` `the absence is in connection with the death of the person's partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom the person was responsible` `the absence is in connection with the death of a close relative of the person, or of their partner or of a child or qualifying young person for whom the person or their partner was responsible` `the Secretary of State considers that it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return to Great Britain within the first month` MEANS
    IF (((`the absence is in connection with the death of the person's partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom the person was responsible`)
         OR (`the absence is in connection with the death of a close relative of the person, or of their partner or of a child or qualifying young person for whom the person or their partner was responsible`))
        AND (`the Secretary of State considers that it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return to Great Britain within the first month`))
    THEN 2
    ELSE 1

-- (3) The absence is not expected to exceed, and does not exceed, 6 months and is solely in connection with (a) the person undergoing
-- treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment by or under the supervision of a qualified practitioner, or medically
-- approved convalescence or care as a result of treatment for an illness or impairment the person had before leaving Great Britain;
-- or (b) the person accompanying their partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom they are responsible for treatment or
-- convalescence or care as in (a).
-- src:296 | (3) This paragraph applies where the absence is not expected to exceed, and does not exceed, 6 months and is solely in connection with—
-- src:297 | (a) the person undergoing—
-- src:298 | (i) treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment by, or under the supervision of, a qualified practitioner, or
-- src:299 | (ii) medically approved convalescence or care as a result of treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment, where the person had that illness or impairment before leaving Great Britain; or
-- src:300 | (b) the person accompanying their partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom they are responsible for treatment or convalescence or care as mentioned in sub-paragraph (a).
@ref reg 11(3) (src:296-300)
DECLARE `Reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain` HAS
    `the absence is solely in connection with the person undergoing treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment by, or under the supervision of, a qualified practitioner`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the absence is solely in connection with the person undergoing medically approved convalescence or care as a result of treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment, where the person had that illness or impairment before leaving Great Britain`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the absence is solely in connection with the person accompanying their partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom they are responsible for treatment or convalescence or care as mentioned in sub-paragraph (a)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a mariner`                                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a continental shelf worker who is in a designated area or a prescribed area`              IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:296 | (3) This paragraph applies where the absence is not expected to exceed, and does not exceed, 6 months and is solely in connection with—
-- src:297 | (a) the person undergoing—
-- src:298 | (i) treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment by, or under the supervision of, a qualified practitioner, or
-- src:299 | (ii) medically approved convalescence or care as a result of treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment, where the person had that illness or impairment before leaving Great Britain; or
-- src:300 | (b) the person accompanying their partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom they are responsible for treatment or convalescence or care as mentioned in sub-paragraph (a).
@ref reg 11(3) (src:296-300)
GIVEN absence IS AN `Absence that is measured against a limit`
      reason IS A `Reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 11(3) — paragraph (3) applies` absence reason MEANS
    (`uc1 — the absence is not expected to exceed and does not exceed a time limit` absence (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months))
    AND ((reason's `the absence is solely in connection with the person undergoing treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment by, or under the supervision of, a qualified practitioner`)
         OR (reason's `the absence is solely in connection with the person undergoing medically approved convalescence or care as a result of treatment for an illness or physical or mental impairment, where the person had that illness or impairment before leaving Great Britain`)
         OR (reason's `the absence is solely in connection with the person accompanying their partner or a child or qualifying young person for whom they are responsible for treatment or convalescence or care as mentioned in sub-paragraph (a)`))

-- (4) The absence is not expected to exceed, and does not exceed, 6 months and the person is a mariner or a continental shelf worker
-- who is in a designated area or a prescribed area.
-- src:301 | (4) This paragraph applies where the absence is not expected to exceed, and does not exceed, 6 months and the person is—
-- src:302 | (a) a mariner; or
-- src:303 | (b) a continental shelf worker who is in a designated area or a prescribed area.
@ref reg 11(4) (src:301-303)
GIVEN absence IS AN `Absence that is measured against a limit`
      reason IS A `Reason for a temporary absence from Great Britain`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 11(4) — paragraph (4) applies` absence reason MEANS
    (`uc1 — the absence is not expected to exceed and does not exceed a time limit` absence (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months))
    AND ((reason's `the person is a mariner`)
         OR (reason's `the person is a continental shelf worker who is in a designated area or a prescribed area`))

-- (4A) The person was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government advised
-- British nationals to leave it or arranged their evacuation; paragraph (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (2) applied to them when the
-- information was issued or the evacuation began; the Secretary of State is satisfied it would be unreasonable to expect them to
-- return, or to have returned; and they did not enter the country or territory after the advice to leave.
-- src:304 | (4A) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:305 | (a) the person was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty’s Government—
-- src:306 | (i) provided public information to advise British nationals to leave that country or territory, or
-- src:307 | (ii) arranged the evacuation of British nationals from that country or territory;
-- src:308 | (b) paragraphs (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (2) applied to the person when the public information was issued or the evacuation began;
-- src:309 | (c) the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain; and
-- src:310 | (d) the person did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty’s Government’s public information was to advise British nationals to leave that country or territory.
@ref reg 11(4A) (src:304-310)
DECLARE `Person who may be within regulation 11(4A)` HAS
    `the person was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it, or arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `paragraphs (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (2) applied to the person when the public information was issued or the evacuation began`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:304 | (4A) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:305 | (a) the person was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty’s Government—
-- src:306 | (i) provided public information to advise British nationals to leave that country or territory, or
-- src:307 | (ii) arranged the evacuation of British nationals from that country or territory;
-- src:308 | (b) paragraphs (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (2) applied to the person when the public information was issued or the evacuation began;
-- src:309 | (c) the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain; and
-- src:310 | (d) the person did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty’s Government’s public information was to advise British nationals to leave that country or territory.
@ref reg 11(4A) (src:304-310)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be within regulation 11(4A)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 11(4A) — paragraph (4A) applies` person MEANS
    (person's `the person was present in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it, or arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it`)
    AND (person's `paragraphs (1)(a), (b)(i), (b)(ii) or (2) applied to the person when the public information was issued or the evacuation began`)
    AND (person's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to expect the person to return, or to have returned, to Great Britain`)
    AND (person's `the person did not enter that country or territory when His Majesty's Government's public information was to advise British nationals to leave it`)

-- (1) A temporary absence is disregarded if the person is entitled to universal credit immediately before it began and (b) the absence
-- is not expected to exceed, and does not exceed, one month (two months with paragraph (2)), or paragraph (3) or (4) applies, or
-- paragraph (4A) applies. (4B) The total period of absence disregarded will not exceed 6 months: the absence is counted as one
-- from its first day, and it stops being disregarded once it has lasted beyond 6 months (fork F-11-4B, assumed and not ruled).
-- src:286 | (1) A person's temporary absence from Great Britain is disregarded in determining whether they meet the basic condition to be in Great Britain if—
-- src:287 | (a) the person is entitled to universal credit immediately before the beginning of the period of temporary absence; and
-- src:288 | (b) either—
-- src:289 | (i) the absence is not expected to exceed, and does not exceed, one month, or
-- src:290 | (ii) paragraph (3) or (4) applies , or
-- src:291 | (iii) paragraph (4A) applies.
-- src:311 | (4B) Where a person is temporarily absent from Great Britain, the total period of absence disregarded in determining whether they meet the basic condition to be in Great Britain will not exceed 6 months.
@ref reg 11(1) and (4B) (src:286-311)
GIVEN absence IS AN `Absence that is measured against a limit`
      `the person is entitled to universal credit immediately before the beginning of the period of temporary absence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months of absence that may be disregarded under paragraph (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `paragraph (3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (4A) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 11 — the temporary absence is disregarded` absence `the person is entitled to universal credit immediately before the beginning of the period of temporary absence` `the months of absence that may be disregarded under paragraph (2)` `paragraph (3) applies` `paragraph (4) applies` `paragraph (4A) applies` MEANS
    (`the person is entitled to universal credit immediately before the beginning of the period of temporary absence`)
    AND (`not expected to exceed the months allowed` OR `paragraph (3) applies` OR `paragraph (4) applies` OR `paragraph (4A) applies`)
    AND (NOT (`uc1 — the absence has lasted beyond a day` absence
                (`core — the date reached by adding a time limit to a date` (absence's `first day of the absence`) (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months))))
    WHERE
        `not expected to exceed the months allowed` MEANS
            `uc1 — the absence is not expected to exceed and does not exceed a time limit` absence
                (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS `the months of absence that may be disregarded under paragraph (2)`, unit IS months)
